WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.267 --> 00:00:06.006
"Tackling the Root Cause of Obesity
Without Drugs Like Ozempic"

00:00:07.608 --> 00:00:09.743
Introducing a temporary
weight-loss fix

00:00:09.743 --> 00:00:12.212
using GLP-1 drugs like Ozempic,

00:00:12.212 --> 00:00:14.615
without consideration
of their wider implications

00:00:14.615 --> 00:00:15.716
and a long-term plan,

00:00:15.716 --> 00:00:19.553
has been likened to sprinkling
water on a raging blaze.

00:00:19.553 --> 00:00:22.289
The war against obesity
cannot be won without measures

00:00:22.289 --> 00:00:24.992
to prevent obesity
in the first place.

00:00:24.992 --> 00:00:27.527
That means tackling
the food environment,

00:00:27.527 --> 00:00:30.864
which is based on high-calorie,
fatty, salty, sugary junk,

00:00:30.864 --> 00:00:32.266
rather than relying
on medication

00:00:32.266 --> 00:00:35.836
as a "damage limitation
exercise."

00:00:35.836 --> 00:00:39.506
Yeah, but limiting damage
is a good thing.

00:00:39.506 --> 00:00:41.608
Sure, these drugs may not make
much of a dent

00:00:41.608 --> 00:00:43.176
on a population scale,

00:00:43.176 --> 00:00:46.747
but what about
on an individual basis?

00:00:46.747 --> 00:00:48.882
It’d be great if people ate
healthfully enough

00:00:48.882 --> 00:00:50.517
to prevent and treat
heart disease,

00:00:50.517 --> 00:00:52.552
high blood pressure,
and diabetes too,

00:00:52.552 --> 00:00:54.054
but until that happens,

00:00:54.054 --> 00:00:57.791
drugs for those conditions
can literally be life saving.

00:00:57.791 --> 00:01:01.728
Obesity so dramatically
decreases one’s lifespan--

00:01:01.728 --> 00:01:04.564
reducing life expectancy
as much as a decade--

00:01:04.564 --> 00:01:07.668
that these GLP-1 drugs--
like bariatric surgery--

00:01:07.668 --> 00:01:10.170
should be considered
as a last resort

00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:12.773
for those unwilling
or unable to treat

00:01:12.773 --> 00:01:15.309
the cause of their obesity.

00:01:15.309 --> 00:01:16.810
Put diabetics on Ozempic,

00:01:16.810 --> 00:01:19.413
and they eat less
high-fat and sweet foods.

00:01:19.413 --> 00:01:21.014
Put nondiabetics on Ozempic,

00:01:21.014 --> 00:01:23.650
and they eat less high-fat
and non-sweet foods.

00:01:23.650 --> 00:01:25.218
So, diabetics on Ozempic

00:01:25.218 --> 00:01:27.120
are eating fewer
pastries and doughnuts,

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:28.655
and nondiabetics on Ozempic

00:01:28.655 --> 00:01:31.591
are eating fewer ham, cheese,
and sausage sandwiches.

00:01:31.591 --> 00:01:35.462
The problem
is people eat too much crap;

00:01:35.462 --> 00:01:37.764
so, anything that gets people
to eat less crap

00:01:37.764 --> 00:01:39.132
can be beneficial,

00:01:39.132 --> 00:01:41.969
including surgically rearranging
our digestive organs

00:01:41.969 --> 00:01:43.570
with bariatric surgery.

00:01:43.570 --> 00:01:45.405
But we don’t need
to go under the knife

00:01:45.405 --> 00:01:50.510
or take a $1,000-a-month drug
to de-crap our diet.

00:01:50.510 --> 00:01:52.412
But what about the cravings,
though?

00:01:52.412 --> 00:01:54.047
The obesogenic environment--

00:01:54.047 --> 00:01:57.050
that is, the obesity-generating
toxic food environment--

00:01:57.050 --> 00:01:59.353
can overwhelm
even substantial efforts

00:01:59.353 --> 00:02:02.589
to enact individual
behavioral changes.

00:02:02.589 --> 00:02:05.592
After ramping up for three
months to high-dose Ozempic,

00:02:05.592 --> 00:02:07.928
people are able
to cut nearly 1,000 calories

00:02:07.928 --> 00:02:09.229
out of their daily diet.

00:02:09.229 --> 00:02:12.032
How could you possibly do that
without drugs,

00:02:12.032 --> 00:02:13.533
unless you were on some kind

00:02:13.533 --> 00:02:14.835
of liquid diet
meal-replacement shakes

00:02:14.835 --> 00:02:16.436
or something?

00:02:16.436 --> 00:02:20.540
Or, you could eat
a diet centered around

00:02:20.540 --> 00:02:22.509
the healthiest foods
on the planet.

00:02:22.509 --> 00:02:25.746
If you put people on a diet
packed with fruits, vegetables,

00:02:25.746 --> 00:02:27.014
whole grains, and beans,

00:02:27.014 --> 00:02:29.449
and allow them to eat
as much as they want,

00:02:29.449 --> 00:02:33.520
they end up eating about
50 percent fewer calories

00:02:33.520 --> 00:02:34.755
than they might have otherwise.

00:02:34.755 --> 00:02:37.491
Just as full,
on half the calories.

00:02:37.491 --> 00:02:40.327
Wait. How can people be
satisfied after cutting

00:02:40.327 --> 00:02:43.363
more than 1,000 calories
out of their daily diets?

00:02:43.363 --> 00:02:46.800
By eating more high-bulk,
low-calorie-density foods

00:02:46.800 --> 00:02:49.636
(vegetables, fruits,
whole grains, and beans)

00:02:49.636 --> 00:02:51.238
and fewer calorie-dense foods,

00:02:51.238 --> 00:02:54.007
like meats, cheeses,
sugars, and fats.

00:02:54.007 --> 00:02:56.743
No wonder a whole food
plant-based diet apparently

00:02:56.743 --> 00:03:00.781
achieved greater weight loss
than any other diet.

00:03:00.781 --> 00:03:04.951
So, could good nutrition present
a safer and cheaper approach

00:03:04.951 --> 00:03:07.054
to weight loss
for most patients?

00:03:07.054 --> 00:03:09.222
Not only can the ingestion
of a plant-based meal

00:03:09.222 --> 00:03:11.124
more than double
GLP-1 secretion,

00:03:11.124 --> 00:03:12.826
compared to
a same-calorie meat meal,

00:03:12.826 --> 00:03:14.928
but plant-based diets
can also cause weight loss

00:03:14.928 --> 00:03:17.931
by virtue of calorie-trapping,
high-fiber foods,

00:03:17.931 --> 00:03:19.466
which flush calories away,

00:03:19.466 --> 00:03:21.535
or by boosting
our resting metabolic rate,

00:03:21.535 --> 00:03:22.669
which helps explain

00:03:22.669 --> 00:03:24.971
why the largest study
of vegans to date

00:03:24.971 --> 00:03:26.706
showed that those eating
strictly plant-based diets

00:03:26.706 --> 00:03:29.709
are about 35 pounds (16 kg)
lighter, on average.

00:03:29.709 --> 00:03:31.978
One randomized trial found
that a strictly plant-based diet

00:03:31.978 --> 00:03:35.982
may reduce annual food costs
by about $500.

00:03:35.982 --> 00:03:37.851
Healthier, more plant-based,
diets may be about

00:03:37.851 --> 00:03:40.587
25 percent less expensive.

00:03:40.587 --> 00:03:44.091
And eating groats and greens,

00:03:44.091 --> 00:03:47.094
maybe even spicy
groats and greens,

00:03:47.094 --> 00:03:50.230
may be able to provide
an extra GLP-1 boost.

00:03:50.230 --> 00:03:51.665
For more healthy
weight-loss tips,

00:03:51.665 --> 00:03:53.800
check out my evidence-based
weight-loss book,

00:03:53.800 --> 00:03:58.004
for which all proceeds I receive
are donated to charity.

00:03:58.004 --> 00:03:59.773
The Drug and Therapeutics
Bulletin,

00:03:59.773 --> 00:04:01.408
which is also independent

00:04:01.408 --> 00:04:03.276
and doesn’t accept
any advertising,

00:04:03.276 --> 00:04:05.345
concluded that more data
on Ozempic’s

00:04:05.345 --> 00:04:07.447
long-term safety and efficacy
are needed

00:04:07.447 --> 00:04:09.883
before it can be recommended
for routine use

00:04:09.883 --> 00:04:11.651
for the treatment of obesity,

00:04:11.651 --> 00:04:13.987
reminding readers
that historically,

00:04:13.987 --> 00:04:16.256
nearly all the drugs
approved for weight loss

00:04:16.256 --> 00:04:18.024
have later been
pulled from the market

00:04:18.024 --> 00:04:20.227
because of safety concerns.

00:04:20.227 --> 00:04:21.428
But wait.

00:04:21.428 --> 00:04:24.764
Obesity so dramatically
decreases one’s lifespan

00:04:24.764 --> 00:04:25.832
that even if these drugs

00:04:25.832 --> 00:04:28.235
ended up shaving years
off of people’s lives,

00:04:28.235 --> 00:04:30.237
wouldn’t they still be worth it?

00:04:30.237 --> 00:04:34.174
Well, that assumes
these drugs cure obesity,

00:04:34.174 --> 00:04:37.110
but if you remember from
the drug’s own package insert,

00:04:37.110 --> 00:04:38.578
in all the major trials,

00:04:38.578 --> 00:04:41.715
people started out obese
and ended up obese,

00:04:41.715 --> 00:04:43.783
after the drugs effectively
stopped working

00:04:43.783 --> 00:04:45.819
and body weight plateaus.

00:04:45.819 --> 00:04:48.388
Then, you’re paying to take the
drug for the rest of your life

00:04:48.388 --> 00:04:51.191
just so you don’t lose ground
and re-gain everything,

00:04:51.191 --> 00:04:54.861
while continuing to face any
and all long-term side effects.

00:04:54.861 --> 00:04:57.330
Historically, the medical
profession has offered

00:04:57.330 --> 00:04:59.666
a sorry collection of harmful

00:04:59.666 --> 00:05:02.502
or downright dangerous
weight-loss interventions.

00:05:02.502 --> 00:05:04.471
Caution about
long-term side effects is,

00:05:04.471 --> 00:05:06.006
therefore, warranted.

00:05:06.006 --> 00:05:09.309
If you look at
the post-approval withdrawal

00:05:09.309 --> 00:05:10.810
of anti-obesity drugs,

00:05:10.810 --> 00:05:13.046
pulled from the market
because of safety concerns

00:05:13.046 --> 00:05:14.981
only discovered years later,

00:05:14.981 --> 00:05:19.753
it took an average of a decade
before dangers came to light,

00:05:19.753 --> 00:05:21.154
and in one case,

00:05:21.154 --> 00:05:22.455
we didn’t discover
a weight-loss drug’s

00:05:22.455 --> 00:05:23.857
long-term adverse effects

00:05:23.857 --> 00:05:26.626
until 38 years
after it hit the market.

00:05:26.626 --> 00:05:29.529
What’s more, even after
that first report of danger,

00:05:29.529 --> 00:05:31.464
it takes an average
of another decade

00:05:31.464 --> 00:05:33.433
to actually get it banned.

00:05:33.433 --> 00:05:35.569
It can even take as long as
another two decades,

00:05:35.569 --> 00:05:38.438
even though people died
in about a quarter of cases.

00:05:38.438 --> 00:05:42.075
As one critic said about how
long it takes regulators to act:

00:05:42.075 --> 00:05:44.544
"It would probably
take the system 2 years

00:05:44.544 --> 00:05:47.614
to ban cyanide.”

00:05:47.614 --> 00:05:50.350
Just recently,
a French drug maker was fined

00:05:50.350 --> 00:05:52.385
nearly half a billion dollars

00:05:52.385 --> 00:05:54.454
for fraudulently
and relentlessly promoting

00:05:54.454 --> 00:05:56.389
its appetite-suppressing
weight-loss drug

00:05:56.389 --> 00:05:58.525
while covering up known harms,

00:05:58.525 --> 00:06:02.829
causing hundreds or thousands to
die from heart valve problems.

00:06:02.829 --> 00:06:05.265
At least it learned its lesson,
though.

00:06:05.265 --> 00:06:08.935
I mean, what other drug company
would conceal the harms

00:06:08.935 --> 00:06:12.105
of appetite suppressors
after a fine that big?

00:06:12.105 --> 00:06:16.142
After all, it was only making up
to 20 million euros a year.

00:06:16.142 --> 00:06:20.247
Let me do the math real quick...

00:06:20.247 --> 00:06:22.582
That’ll teach ’em!

00:06:22.582 --> 00:06:24.217
These days, GLP-1 drug makers

00:06:24.217 --> 00:06:26.453
are worth more
than a trillion dollars.

00:06:26.453 --> 00:06:30.457
I’m sure they would never try
to cover anything up.

